169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (Every space carries within it an invisible architecture of expectation. Long before a visitor steps through the door, decisions have already been made on their behalf: what they should notice, how long they should linger, what counts as meaningful. These decisions belong, almost exclusively, to the institution. The people who build the world inside the walls are the same people who quietly decide how that world ought to be inhabited. And so a hierarchy is born, rarely spoken aloud but felt in every sign, every rope barrier, every carefully worded label.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (This is the institution's dream of the visitor: attentive, unhurried, pausing at each label, departing enriched. It is not an ignoble dream. But it is, for the vast majority of actual visitors on any actual day, almost entirely fictional.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
