/E (Every space carries within it an invisible architecture of expectation. Long before a visitor steps through the door, decisions have already been made on their behalf: what they should notice, how long they should linger, what counts as meaningful. These decisions belong, almost exclusively, to the institution. The people who build the world inside the walls are the same people who quietly decide how that world ought to be inhabited.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0]
>>
