/E (There is a particular silence that settles over a well-designed gallery. Hushed, reverent, deliberate. A silence that says: this is a serious place, and seriousness is expected of you. Beneath the posted rules and careful arrangements lies an unwritten contract: pay attention to what we have prepared for you. This is the institution's dream of the visitor. And it is, for the vast majority of actual people on any actual day, almost entirely fictional.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
